              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Historical Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "report other neurologic abnormalities such as",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Historical Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "ataxia, seizures, or behavior changes.",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Historical Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Papilledema—no clinically detectable visual",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Historical Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "abnormalities but may report other neuro-",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Historical Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "logic abnormalities attributable to increased",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Historical Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "ICP.",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Historical Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Physical Examination Findings",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Optic neuritis—may be unilateral or",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "bilateral; absent menace response, absent",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "dazzle, mydriatic and nonresponsive pupil;",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "may have anisocoria if unilaterally affected.",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Usually, the anterior segment appears normal,",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "but hyperemia, congestion, and hemorrhages",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "of the optic nerve head are seen. The retina",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "surrounding the optic nerve may be detached;",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "chorioretinitis can occur concurrently.",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 1,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Papilledema—usually bilateral, menace",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Electroretinogram—investigate retinal",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "response is present, dazzle is present, normal",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "function; normal in patients with optic",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "pupillary light reflexes. The anterior segment",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "neuritis and papilledema, flat in those with",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "appears normal, but there is swelling and",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "SARDS.",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "elevation of optic nerve head with loss of the",
              "pdf_page": 1080,
              "printed_page": 998,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Physical Examination Findings"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Measure ICP.",
